# hamotazky.cz

> Free website for learning the official question set of the Czech amateur radio operator licence exam, run by the Czech Telecommunication Office (ČTÚ), for operator classes A (HAREC) and N (NOVICE). Questions can be browsed with their correct answers, practised by topic and tried in a mock exam scored by the same criteria as the real one. The question data is also published through a public REST API and as JSON and SQLite downloads.

- The website is in Czech.
- The questions match the current official question set published by ČTÚ.
- ČTÚ publishes only the correct answers. The wrong answer options on this site are indicative only and may differ from the real exam.
- Class A (HAREC) allows operating on all permitted amateur bands with higher power, class N (NOVICE) is an entry level class with restrictions. Upgrading from N to A later means taking the full class A exam again, not only the difference, so the site recommends going straight for class A.
- The exam has three parts (radio regulations, radio operating practice, electrical and radio engineering) and each part has to be passed separately.

